{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":751,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.14","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 14","reference":"Psalms 14","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The atheism and corruption of mankind, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-3.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"An expostulation with sinners, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"4-6.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"A prayer for the salvation of God, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"To the chief musician, A psalm of David.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"The fool - The wicked man.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"Good - That is, actions really good or pleasing to God.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":11,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":12,"text":"Looked - God knoweth all things without any enquiry: but he speaks after the manner of men.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":13,"text":"Upon - Upon the whole Israelitish nation, and upon all mankind for he speaks of all except his people, and the righteous ones, who are opposed to these, ver.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":14,"text":"4, 5.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":15,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":16,"text":"Gone - From God, and from the rule which he hath given them.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":17,"text":"Filthy - Loathsome and abominable to God.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":18,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":19,"text":"Bread - With as little remorse, and with as much greediness.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":20,"text":"Call not - They are guilty not only of gross injustice towards men, but also of horrid impiety and contempt of God.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":21,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":22,"text":"There - Upon the spot, where they practiced these insolences, God struck them with a panick fear.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":23,"text":"For - God is on their side, and therefore their enemies have cause to tremble.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":24,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":25,"text":"Because - This was the ground of their contempt, that he lived by faith in God's promise and providence.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":26,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":27,"text":"O that - These words immediately concern the deliverance of Israel out of that sinful state, in which they now were; which having described, he concludes, with a prayer to God to help them out of Zion, where the ark then was, but principally they design the spiritual redemption and salvation of all God's Israel by the Messiah.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":28,"text":"The captivity - His captive people.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":29,"text":"The children of Jacob, as Aaron is named for his sons, 1 Chron. xii, 27.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":14}}